//! Chrysalis: Inside a ship's purple hold, 44 by 28 m and round at both ends under a barrel vault and two half domes, mirrored red (-x) to blue (+x). In the middle a chrysalis hangs from the vault on its spine; top mid is a ring round the spine 3.5 m up, its hole over the pit, a lift from the pit. Each base is a round pod against its end wall: arched doors to the hall and the north lane, a lift up through its roof, a gallery curving north from its roof to the ring, and a ramp spiralling down its south side to the south lane.
